            <ArticleTitle>[Retrograde perfusion of the coronary sinus].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>219-23</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The investigations by Ratajczak-Pakalska showed peculiarities of cardiac venous circulation which make retrograde perfusion possible. Microcirculation is flowing in two directions, especially in diffuse cardiosclerosis. The results of the authors' animal experiments prove that the method of retrograde perfusion of coronary veins might be used ultimately in these cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
